-- title:
--   Explicit dyadic chirp data for the 16384-point high-height evaluator
-- statement:
--   Transparent finite data only: 112-bit intermediate sine/cosine integers and 80-bit final complex dyadic proposals for the 5463 reduced square-residue arguments needed by a 16384-point chirp transform. The mask records needed arguments; unused entries are zero. No analytic enclosure or RH assertion is made by this definition.
-- source:
--   Platt, Isolating some non-trivial zeros of zeta, DOI 10.1090/mcom/3198, FFT architecture. Chirp/Bluestein exact-convolution representation with ordinary integer Taylor arithmetic and dyadic rounding. Surrounding mathematical attribution: sometik179, c9908072-d99a-4431-aad8-a72c6352619a, Gabewhigham. The pi seed is taken from the accepted 700-decimal Machin enclosure. Original recovered workspace and accepted low-height proof data are unchanged.

